---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AboutPhoto from './AboutPhoto.astro';
import AboutIllustration from './AboutIllustration.astro';
import AboutClosing from './AboutClosing.astro';
import '../styles/about-redesign.css';
const scope=[['Machining, material & finish','Drawing revision, grade, quantity, quoted work and approved alternatives.'],['Inspection & records','Critical features, sampling, report scope and material documentation.'],['Separate charges','Tooling, special documentation, freight and duties where applicable.'],['Payment & sample charges','Payment method, currency, stages and amounts; sample machining, setup and freight, including any agreed credit toward a later order.']];
---
<Layout title="How we work: drawing review to CNC parts delivery" description="Follow LZZ's order process: drawing review, quotation, sample approval, production, inspection, packing and delivery responsibilities." cta={false} articleImage="/media/about-redesign-20261014/drawing-review-1200.webp">
 <article class="al-page al-workflow"><div class="al-wrap">
  <header class="al-hero"><div class="al-split-hero"><div><h1>From drawing review<br/>to finished parts.</h1><p class="al-lead">We review your drawing for quotation, then agree sample approval, production and delivery. A clear revision and acceptance plan carry the requirements from the first discussion to the finished parts.</p></div><AboutIllustration kind="drawing" eager/></div><dl class="al-order-facts" id="ww-before-title"><div><dt>Minimum order</dt><dd>From 1 piece</dd></div><div><dt>Production</dt><dd>7-14 business days</dd><p>After drawing and order confirmation, including surface finishing.</p></div><div><dt>Shipping and commercial terms</dt><dd>Agreed for the order</dd><p>Transit time is additional. Confirm payment and sample charges in the quotation.</p></div></dl></header>
  <section class="al-section" id="quotation-scope"><span id="ww-define-title"/><span id="section-3"/><header class="al-section-head"><h2>Start with a consistent drawing and quotation</h2><p>Send the drawing revision, material, quantity, part function and required date. For a sample, identify what to retain or change and agree the measurement and drawing work.</p></header><div class="al-quote-grid"><div><h3>Define what controls the part</h3><p>Include the model and a controlled drawing for critical dimensions, fits, finishes and inspection requirements. If the files disagree, identify which takes precedence.</p><p>Any proposed changes to geometry or setup need your approval before production.</p><nav class="al-actions"><a class="al-inline-link" href="/resources/ordering/rfq-checklist/">Prepare your RFQ package</a></nav></div><div id="section-4"><h3>Review the complete quoted scope</h3><dl class="al-scope-list">{scope.map(([title,text])=><div><dt>{title}</dt><dd>{text}</dd></div>)}</dl><span id="commercial-terms"/></div></div></section>
  <section class="al-section" id="section-5"><span id="ww-approval-title"/><header class="al-section-head"><h2>Release the approved specification for production</h2><p>Agree sample acceptance before machining. Carry the approved revision, material and finish into the production order.</p></header><div class="al-release"><div><article class="al-step"><span class="al-step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Check and approve the first sample</h3><p>Agree critical interfaces, appearance and functional tests. Record the first-article approval and the criteria for releasing production.</p><a class="al-inline-link" href="/resources/ordering/machined-prototype-approval-checklist/">Sample approval checklist</a></div></article><article class="al-step" id="section-6"><span class="al-step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Agree batch inspection and records</h3><p>Define sampling, recorded dimensions and material traceability. Confirm the measurement method, report format and handling of nonconforming parts before the batch starts.</p><a class="al-inline-link" href="/factory/#quality">Inspection planning at LZZ</a></div></article></div><AboutPhoto id="cmm-detail" caption="LZZ coordinate measuring machine. Measurement methods and reports are agreed for the order."/></div></section>
  <section class="al-section" id="packaging-shipping"><span id="ww-handover-title"/><header class="al-section-head"><h2>Protect the parts and agree the delivery basis</h2><p>Confirm packing, receiving details and documents alongside the production schedule.</p></header><div class="al-packing"><AboutPhoto id="shipping-example" caption="Protected components in the LZZ packing archive · November 2022"/><div id="section-8"><h3>Packing and identification</h3><p>Select cartons or wooden cases suited to the shipment. Protect cosmetic faces, seals and threads. Specify part number, revision and quantity per pack.</p><h3>Transport and documents</h3><p>Provide the destination and receiving contact. Agree dispatch and arrival dates, transport, Incoterm and costs, including responsibility for customs, duties and taxes.</p><p>Use approved part, revision and order references on the dimensional, material and delivery records.</p><a class="al-inline-link" href="/resources/ordering/custom-cnc-parts-shipping-checklist/">Packing and shipping checklist</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="al-section" id="section-2"><span id="ww-issue-title"/><header class="al-section-head"><h2>Keep changes and acceptance decisions clear</h2><p>Drawing changes and part discrepancies need a documented review against the agreed order requirements.</p></header><div class="al-support"><article><h3>Changes after approval</h3><p>If the drawing or quantity changes, update the quoted work and schedule. A revised drawing may require sample approval again.</p><a class="al-inline-link" href="/resources/ordering/prototype-vs-small-batch-cnc/">Plan prototypes and repeat orders</a></article><article><h3>Nonconforming parts and after-sales terms</h3><p>Send the revision, part or batch reference, affected quantity, photographs and measurements. We review the discrepancy against the agreed criteria.</p><p>Agree warranty period, start date, exclusions and reporting procedure, with responsibility for rework, replacement, return freight and refunds.</p><a class="al-inline-link" href="/about/contact/">Discuss a part discrepancy</a></article></div></section>
  <AboutClosing title="Prepare your machining inquiry" text="Send the controlled drawing, material and quantity, with the features and records needed for acceptance."/>
 </div></article>
</Layout>
